# forge/limb/faceted: faceted limbs (KNAPPED; 28.3): angular plates every four rows: a lit wedge top-left, a dark wedge
# bottom-right, a hard crease between.
# FORGE-MARKS, forge i2 (tools: emb_P2c/forge/areas/FORGE-MARKS/tools2/mk2.py). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# LIMB TILE (`overlay limb.<v>`, a region tile, `on-region`): the body's style on its sleeves and thighs (U F T), the
# gloves' on the cuffs and flares (C X), the boots' on the shins (S). Ink cells move the step by k - 2 (inside 1..4):
# `+` +1, `^` +2, `:` -1, `=` -2; `O` (metal2 2) recolours to Metal 2 keeping the step. Periods 2 or more along one
# axis only (lines and rows, never a checker): a shin is 2-3 px wide, so each limb is one strong motif.
# (FORGE-MARKS forge i3) faceted: period 4 rows, a facet from a glint to its dark crease.
use person
role overlay limb.faceted
tags tile overlay
on-region U F C X T S
legend + ink 3
legend ^ ink 4
legend : ink 1
legend = ink 0
legend O metal2 2
# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i1) faceted: a glass facet per 4 rows: the hard lit edge, the lit face, the plane, its shade (rows only: a 3 px limb takes no diagonal).
# (forge fix i2, MATERIAL; the owner: "Obsidian reads as black cloth": i1's 1-wide tile drew a white row every 4 px across
# every glove and greave, zebra stripes that read as quilted cloth) a glass facet a 4 x 6 cell: a "/" specular streak (+2)
# with its lit flank (+1) on the upper left, a flat dark plane, the lower right a step down (on obsidian the violet rim).

# (envelope r1, FORGE-MATERIAL; A4 "no 1 px streak anywhere", A8) the facet as planes, rows only: a 2 x 2 lit face at
# the top left (+1: the light's facet), two rows of dark glass, a 2 x 2 shade at the lower right (-1), so a 2-3 px greave
# reads lit block / black glass / shade block, never a "/" of single pixels; the specular is the glass pass's stamp
# (maps/forge/glass), placed by the compositor on facets of 4 px or more.
view D key rest origin 0 0
